GPRAY
syntax: gpray <text>
Syntax: Gpray ++

Priests who have trained themselves to maximum benefit before their gods may
utilize a priest specific ability to 'god' pray, or gpray.  By using gpray,
a priest may send a prayer specifically to their god.  The gpray is much
like a regular prayer, except that it is stored for whichever god the given
priest prays to.

If a priest wishes to write a longer prayer than what is allowed by the
limit of the input, may type gpray ++ to enter a string editor. There
they will be able to write fairly long prayers. When you wish to exit this
editor, simply type '@' on an empty line and it will exit the string editor.
Your prayer will be sent to the Gods automatically.

Priests wishing to send a prayer to their god in this manner can send a
gpray that is anywhere from one line to four lines long, and it is
recommended that they do not spam their gods with the same prayers over and
over.

Be wary, there have been rumors that priests who are in the midst of
composing notes of any kind that suddenly decide to gpray to their god may
lose their concentration and find that their notes have been wiped clean.

Example:

Gpray I am your humble servant. Do with me as you will.
-- will send a one line prayer to your God.

gpray ++
I am your humble servant.
Do with me as you will.
Love <name>
@
-- Will send a -multi-line prayer to your God, much like a normal note.

See also - PRIEST PRAY
